      ":question/problem": "Find the antiderivative of\n$\\frac{6}{x^{5}}+2\\sqrt[5]{x^{4}}+x^{2}.$ For real $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int\\left(\\frac{6}{x^{5}}+2\\sqrt[5]{x^{4}}+x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= \\int\\left(6x^{-5}+2x^{\\frac{4}{5}}+x^{2}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 6\\int x^{-5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+2\\int x^{\\frac{4}{5}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x+\\int x^{2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\ &= 6\\left(\\frac{x^{-5+1}}{(-5+1)}\\right)+2\\left(\\frac{x^{\\frac{4}{5}+1}}{(\\frac{4}{5}+1)}\\right)\\\\ &\\quad +\\left(\\frac{x^{2+1}}{(2+1)}\\right)+C\\\\ &= -\\frac{3}{2x^{4}}+\\frac{10\\sqrt[5]{x^{9}}}{9}+\\frac{x^{3}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
